          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em line integral
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            along a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curve"} curve
            %em path integrals
            (not to be confused with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contour+integrals"} contour integrals
            (especially in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analysis"} complex analysis
          %p
            By the modern understanding of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration of differential forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-forms"} differential 1-forms
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+vector+fields"}> cotangent vector fields
            ) along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curves"} curves
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoform"} pseudo
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p Here we assume familiarity with integration of differential forms and pseudoforms, defining in terms of them the various classical notions of line integral.
          %p
            In each case, the classical notation (developed before the rigorous treatment of analysis in the 19th century) is not taken literally by the classical definition (developed after the rigorous treatment and still found in calculus texts), and this definition is accompanied by a
            %span.newWikiWord
              reparametrisation
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/parametrization"} ?
            theorem. We would like to make sense of the classical notation and eliminate the reparametrisation theorems (or at least make them all special cases of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "differential+form#IntegrationTheorem"} a general theorem to be proved once for all
          %h3#line_integral_of_a_vector_field Line integral of a vector field
          %p
            Classically, we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec{F}\colon X \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuously+differentiable+map"} continuously differentiable map
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\colon [a,b] \to X
            %strong line integral
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec{F}
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is defined as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mover
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ≔
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
